<div id="recipe-87435-instructions" class="wprm-recipe-instructions-container wprm-recipe-87435-instructions-container wprm-block-text-normal" data-recipe="87435"><h3 class="wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-instructions-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-none" style="">Instructions</h3><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-group"><ul class="wprm-recipe-instructions"><li id="wprm-recipe-87435-step-0-0" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;">Preheat oven to 400 &deg;F (204 &deg;C). Line a baking sheet with parchment paper and set it aside.</div></li><li id="wprm-recipe-87435-step-0-1" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;">Using a pair of kitchen scissors or a sharp chef&rsquo;s knife, split each pita open along the pocket seam into two thin rounds.</div></li><li id="wprm-recipe-87435-step-0-2" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;">Brush each piece with olive oil and sprinkle it with salt on both sides. I used about 1 tablespoon of olive oil and &frac14;  teaspoon of salt per pita.</div></li><li id="wprm-recipe-87435-step-0-3" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;">Stack them on top of each other and cut into 8 triangles.</div></li><li id="wprm-recipe-87435-step-0-4" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;">Spread them on the prepared baking sheet in a single layer, ensuring that they don&rsquo;t overlap.</div></li><li id="wprm-recipe-87435-step-0-5" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;">Bake 8 to 10 minutes, flipping them halfway through to ensure even baking.</div></li><li id="wprm-recipe-87435-step-0-6" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;"><span style="display: block;">Let them cool for 10 minutes before serving.</span></div></li></ul></div></div>
